Article 27
(1) Funding for the implementation of protection for women and children includes:
a. prevention of violence against women and children;
b. service institutions including service facilities and infrastructure;
c. medical services, which include doctor examinations, treatment costs, hospital costs, medication costs and medical support costs;
d. medicolegal services, which include examinations for visum et repertum, visum et repertum psikiatrikum, and Deoxyribonucleic Acid tests;
e. psychosocial services, which consist of counseling and psychological therapy, safe houses and safe house management;
f. legal services and assistance including costs of accompaniment at the police, prosecutor's office, and court;
g. operational costs of service institutions, including outreach transportation, accompaniment transportation, and fulfillment of victims' needs while at the service institution; and
h. service institution officers, including honorarium and capacity building.
(2) Management of funding as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

