g. funding.

Article 3
The Implementation of Protection of Women and Children aims to: a. prevent acts of violence against women and children; b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect, provide a sense of security for women and children; d. provide services to women victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
e. provide services to children both as victims, witnesses as well as perpetrators of violence;
f. facilitate and conduct mediation on domestic disputes to realize an equal and just household; and g. prioritize services and protection for Vulnerable Groups.

CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTIONAL STRENGTHENING
Article 14
In order to maximize the function and role of service officers, the following are required: a. increasing the number and capacity of human resources of service officers; b. development of communication, information, and education systems regarding protection services for women and children;
c. coordination system between UPT PPA and other service institutions at the Regional level;
d. integrated case data system;
e. system and/or mechanism for case handling and or case assistance; and
f. improvement of service facilities and infrastructure.

CHAPTER V
PROVISION OF SERVICE INSTITUTIONS
Article 6
(1) In the context of providing protection services to women and children, the Regional Government establishes UPT PPA.
(2) UPT PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) carries out the following service functions:
a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
- 6 - (3) In carrying out the service functions as referred to in paragraph (2), UPT PPA requires support for:
a. infrastructure facilities and infrastructure;
b. sufficient number of management personnel;
c. competent human resources;
d. budget; and
e. safe house facilities.
(4) Further provisions regarding the organization and working procedures of UPT PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

